<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every user-facing string in the app [§12, plan 4.4].

  The audit found exactly ONE string here (app_name); everything else — including the text
  printed on customer reports — was hard-coded French inside Kotlin, so localisation was
  impossible without a code rewrite and no string could be reviewed or corrected without
  touching source. French is the default locale (this is a French-market instrument); adding
  a language now means adding a values-xx/ file and nothing else.

  `ci/checks.sh` fails the build if user-facing text reappears as a literal in a Compose file.
-->
